# 🧪 Fix Workflow for Failed Test Case

When a test fails unexpectedly and the cause is unclear, use this structure to fully analyze, isolate, fix, and document the case.

## Fix Summary Log
```yaml
fix_summary:
  test_case: [test name, e.g. test_onboarding_flow]
  failure_signature:
    message: >
      TypeError: Exactly one of the passed values can be specified. Instead, values were: (None,), {'hexstr': None}
    traceback_file: test_onboarding.py
    failure_line: [line number if known]
    system_context: InviteNFT / onboarding / web3.py

  suspected_cause:
    hypothesis: >
      Function returns SignedTransaction instead of tx hash.
    triggering_call: transact_contract_function()
    risk_factor: mismatch with web3.py 7.x expectations

  isolation_test:
    file: test_alarm_mode.py
    name: test_transact_contract_function_receipt_error
    behavior: >
      Confirms that returned object is not a string.
    result: reproduced

  root_cause:
    description: >
        [Describe the exact condition or mismatch that causes the failure.
        Be specific about the code or integration that triggers it.]
    source_file: [path/to/module]
    line_modified: [line number]
    version_note: [if library upgrade is involved, document it]


  fix_action:
    performed_change: >
      Replaced all rawTransaction references with raw_transaction
    validation: ✅ manual retest passed
    regression_check: reran original test → ✅ passed

  post_fix_notes:
    new_test_added: test_transact_contract_function_receipt_error
    log_clean: true
    failure_type: fixed
    lessons_learned:
      - Always check return types of external integrations
      - Validate attribute names during dependency upgrades
      - Isolate test conditions to reproduce complex breakages
